>> title: Thai Red Curry
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, coconut, thai, chiles, curry
>> counters: Thai Kitchen, One Pot
>> aka: gaeng dang, gaeng ped, gaeng pet, kaeng phet, gang ped, red curry, red curry chicken
>> pairs-with: thai-red-curry-paste, coconut-rice
>> servings: 4
>> time: 40 min
>> step.1: crack the cream 5 min
>> step.2: fry the paste 3 min
>> step.3: simmer 12 min
>> step.4: season
>> step.5: stir in

Fry the thick cream spooned off the top of @coconut milk{28%oz}(800 mL; two cans, unshaken) in a #wok{} over medium heat for ~fry{5%min}, until it splits and beads its own oil.

Fry @Thai red curry paste{1/4%cup}(60 g) into @&(~1)cracked cream{} for ~fry{3%min}, pressing it against the pan until the kitchen smells of it and the oil runs red.

Simmer @chicken thighs{1%lb}(450 g; boneless, sliced 1/4-in thick), @bamboo shoots{1%cup}(drained and sliced) and @makrut lime leaves{4}(torn) with @&(~1)fried paste{} and the rest of both cans for ~simmer{12%min}.

Season @&(~1)curry{} with @fish sauce{2%Tbs} and @palm sugar{2%tsp}.

Stir @Thai basil{1%cup}(leaves only) and @red spur chiles{2}(sliced on the diagonal) into @&(~1)curry{} off the heat.
